Description: D(HE)at attack proof-of-concept against TLS and SSH
 D(HE)ater is the proof-of-concept implementation of the D(HE)at attack
 (CVE-2002-20001), a low-bandwidth denial-of-service attack that saturates a
 server's CPU by enforcing Diffie-Hellman ephemeral (DHE) key exchange over
 TLS and SSH.
 .
 It uses CryptoLyzer to detect whether a target supports DHE and to generate
 the handshakes required to perform the attack. The package installs the
 "dheat" command-line tool and the "dh_param_priv_key_size_setter" helper.
 .
 This tool performs a real denial-of-service attack and must only be used
 against systems you own or are explicitly authorized to test.
